From 481a762e06ca8112ecd4c550b9d32b082ae8c2a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liweijie2000 <liweijie39@huawei.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 17:25:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] urma: build main_primary_eid table entries from topology

To avoid repeated main_primary_eid topology traversal, build the EID to main_primary_eid mapping during topology configuration and program the result to ubcore before setting the ubcore topology.

- Keep public insert, batch insert, delete, lookup and flush APIs for the main_primary_eid table.
- Add a topology helper that counts valid endpoint groups, builds a temporary hash table keyed by node index, entity id and chip id to choose the minimum primary EID, and records each valid primary and port EID under that group.
- Pack mappings as group-batch payloads using group metadata plus a contiguous prefixes array, and split requests by the 4096-prefix ioctl limit.
- Add internal UVS ubcore ioctl and TLV support for group-batch programming and topo deletion.

(cherry picked from commit 186cac687904a42f43cb64c3e5c3f424fbe44891)
